  "estimatedMinutes": null,
  "statement": "Find the volume of the three-dimensional solid given by the inequality \\(\\sqrt{x^{2}+y^{2}}+\\) \\(|z| \\leq 1\\).",
  "answerChoices": [],
  "answer": {
    "letter": null,
    "value": null
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.hmmt-feb-guts-2002-p40.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "\\(2 \\pi / 3\\). The solid consists of two cones, one whose base is the circle \\(x^{2}+y^{2}=1\\) in the \\(x y\\)-plane and whose vertex is \\((0,0,1)\\), and the other with the same base but vertex \\((0,0,-1)\\). Each cone has a base area of \\(\\pi\\) and a height of 1 , for a volume of \\(\\pi / 3\\), so the answer is \\(2 \\pi / 3\\).",
